### GOT/PLT Builder - PLT Size Matches Actual Section Data

#### get_plt_size() equals the real create_plt_section_data() byte length

- Verify: get_plt_size() equals the real create_plt_section_data() byte length
   - Expected: builder.get_plt_size() equals `actual_data.len()`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 20 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: get_plt_size() equals the real create_plt_section_data() byte length")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-GotPlt-001
# create_plt_section_data() always prepends the 16-byte PLT[0]
# resolver entry before the per-symbol stubs (see create_plt0_entry).
# get_plt_size() must therefore be (next_plt_index + 1) * 16, not
# next_plt_index * 16 -- otherwise callers who size-allocate the PLT
# section from get_plt_size() under-allocate by one entry (16 bytes).
var builder = GotPltBuilder(
    got_entries: [],
    plt_entries: [],
    got_size: 0,
    plt_size: 0,
    next_got_offset: 0,
    next_plt_index: 0
)
builder.add_symbol("printf")
builder.add_symbol("malloc")
builder.add_symbol("free")
val actual_data = create_plt_section_data(builder)
expect(builder.get_plt_size()).to_equal(actual_data.len())
```

</details>

